Subject: [REVIEW 11/16] Glymur GCC: keep the USB4 router and PHY domains on the wakeup path

Mark gcc_usb4_0_gdsc and gcc_usb_0_phy_gdsc GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP, so they stay on in system sleep while a device in them is on the wakeup path. A router kept across s2idle (patch 16) puts itself and its PHY on that path; a CX power collapse would otherwise take the router state. With no USB4 partner the domains switch off as before. Only router 0 and its PHY are marked.

Dependencies: Patch 02 (same file). Used by patch 16.

Source attribution: Local Surface change (candidate 1.131, kept in the 1.142 implementation).

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
index b5a9036594fedc0f62118e204bb6393bff7fb287..07d0b830def803b6cef3f6194a4523e3ba71556a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
@@ -7734,6 +7734,8 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_usb4_0_gdsc = {
 	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0xf,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_usb4_0_gdsc",
+		/* A router kept across system sleep holds its state here. */
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
@@ -7770,6 +7772,8 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_usb_0_phy_gdsc = {
 	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0x2,
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_usb_0_phy_gdsc",
+		/* And its PHY, which stays initialized with it. */
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
